 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Cracks:** If the octree is not sufficiently adapted to the surface geometry, cracks can appear in the Marching Cubes surface because the method loses guarantees when applied to non-uniform grids [S1].
-*   **Topological Integrity:** Unlike uniform grid methods, octree-based methods do not inherently guarantee watertightness without specific handling of mismatched tree depths at boundaries [S1][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Cracks:** If the octree is not sufficiently adapted to the surface geometry (i.e., adjacent leaf nodes have significantly different depths), cracks may appear in the resulting mesh, particularly with Marching Cubes [S1].
+*   **Loss of Guarantees:** Unlike uniform grids, octree-based methods do not inherently guarantee watertightness or manifold topology without additional constraints or post-processing [S1].
 
